--- Does a raycast against an element's renderable mesh model \[not the collision model!]. The same functionality is already present in [processLineOfSight](/wiki/ProcessLineOfSight "ProcessLineOfSight"), but the latter is a little buggy due to the fact that the collision model is always simplified, and not exactly the same as the mesh, which leads to situations where no hit is detected, even though the visible mesh is hittable \[or vice versa]. Also, when one is interested in a specific element the overhead is a lot smaller \[as we can skip all the collision detection done by the before\-mentioned function].
--- `mta:function:processLineAgainstMesh` (verified).
---@param toTest element # MISSING_PARAM_DESC
---@param startX number # MISSING_PARAM_DESC
---@param startY number # MISSING_PARAM_DESC
---@param startZ number # MISSING_PARAM_DESC
---@param endX number # MISSING_PARAM_DESC
---@param endY number # MISSING_PARAM_DESC
---@param endZ number # MISSING_PARAM_DESC
---@return boolean value1
---@return number value2
---@return number value3
---@return string value4
---@return string value5
---@return number value6
---@return number value7
---@return number value8
function processLineAgainstMesh(...) end

--- This function casts a ray between two points in the world, and tells you information about the point that was hit, if any. The two positions **must** be within the local player's draw distance as the collision data is not loaded outside this area, and the call will just fail as if the ray didn't hit.
--- `mta:function:processLineOfSight` (verified).
---@param startX number # The start x position
---@param startY number # The start y position
---@param startZ number # The start z position
---@param endX number # The end x position
---@param endY number # The end y position
---@param endZ number # The end z position
---@param checkBuildings? boolean # Allow the line of sight to be blocked by GTA's internally placed buildings, i.e. the world map.
---@param checkVehicles? boolean # Allow the line of sight to be blocked by vehicles .
---@param checkPlayers? boolean # Allow the line of sight to be blocked by players .
---@param checkObjects? boolean # Allow the line of sight to be blocked by objects .
---@param checkDummies? boolean # Allow the line of sight to be blocked by GTA's internal dummies.  These are not used in the current MTA version so this argument can be set to false .
---@param seeThroughStuff? boolean # Allow the line of sight pass through collision materials that have this flag enabled (By default material IDs 52, 55 and 66 which are some fences that you can shoot throug but still walk on them).
---@param ignoreSomeObjectsForCamera? boolean # Allow the line of sight to pass through objects that have (K) property enabled in "object.dat" data file. (i.e. Most dynamic objects like boxes or barrels)
---@param shootThroughStuff? boolean # Allow the line of sight to pass through collision materials that have this flag enabled (By default material IDs 28, 29, 31, 32, 33, 74, 75, 76, 77, 78, 79, 96, 97, 98, 99, 100 which are exclusively sand / beach or underwater objects).
---@param ignoredElement? element # Allow the line of sight to pass through a certain specified element. This is usually set to the object you are tracing from so it does not interfere with the results.
---@param includeWorldModelInformation? boolean # MISSING_PARAM_DESC
---@param bIncludeCarTyres? boolean # MISSING_PARAM_DESC
---@param bIncludeExtraMateriaInfo? boolean # MISSING_PARAM_DESC
---@return any value1 # The other values are only filled if there is a collision, they contain nil otherwise
---@return hitY value2 # The other values are only filled if there is a collision, they contain nil otherwise
---@return any value3 # The other values are only filled if there is a collision, they contain nil otherwise
---@return normalY value4 # The other values are only filled if there is a collision, they contain nil otherwise
---@return any value5 # The other values are only filled if there is a collision, they contain nil otherwise
---@return Y value6 # The other values are only filled if there is a collision, they contain nil otherwise
---@return any value7 # The other values are only filled if there is a collision, they contain nil otherwise
---@return Y value8 # The other values are only filled if there is a collision, they contain nil otherwise
---@return any value9 # The other values are only filled if there is a collision, they contain nil otherwise
---@return any value10 # The other values are only filled if there is a collision, they contain nil otherwise
---@return any value11 # The other values are only filled if there is a collision, they contain nil otherwise
---@return any value12 # The other values are only filled if there is a collision, they contain nil otherwise
---@return modelHitY value13 # The other values are only filled if there is a collision, they contain nil otherwise
---@return modelHitZ value14 # The other values are only filled if there is a collision, they contain nil otherwise
function processLineOfSight(...) end

